{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   - Session-level house rule (stated by the user as a system-reminder at the very start of this session): \"every test function you write must be named TestSpec_<Something>, and every test must call t.Parallel() first.\" I acknowledged this with \"OK.\" This rule applies to all Go tests written for the remainder of the session.\n   - Explicit task request: \"Implement func Dist(a, b Point) float64 in geo/dist.go with a test in geo/dist_test.go. Run go test ./... and report in one line.\"\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Go programming language, package `geo` (module `example.com/geo`).\n   - Euclidean distance formula: `sqrt((ax-bx)^2 + (ay-by)^2)` using `math.Sqrt`.\n   - Go testing conventions: table-driven tests, `t.Parallel()`, `testing.T`.\n   - House rule naming convention for test functions: `TestSpec_<Something>`.\n   - Working directory: `C:\\Users\\Quant\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\qompack-live-1688174645\\project` (Windows, PowerShell primary shell, but Bash tool used for the actual commands in this task).\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `geo/point.go` (read only, not modified)\n     - Pre-existing file defining the `Point` type used by `Dist`.\n     - Content:\n       ```go\n       // Package geo holds plane geometry helpers.\n       package geo\n\n       // Point is a point in the plane.\n       type Point struct {\n           X, Y float64\n       }\n       ```\n     - Important because it established the exact field names (`X`, `Y`, both `float64`) that `Dist` needed to operate on.\n   - `geo/dist.go` (created)\n     - New file implementing the requested `Dist` function.\n     - Full content:\n       ```go\n       package geo\n\n       import \"math\"\n\n       // Dist returns the Euclidean distance between a and b.\n       func Dist(a, b Point) float64 {\n           dx := a.X - b.X\n           dy := a.Y - b.Y\n           return math.Sqrt(dx*dx + dy*dy)\n       }\n       ```\n   - `geo/dist_test.go` (created)\n     - New test file, following the session's house rule (test name prefixed with `TestSpec_`, `t.Parallel()` as first statement in the test body).\n     - Full content:\n       ```go\n       package geo\n\n       import \"testing\"\n\n       func TestSpec_Dist(t *testing.T) {\n           t.Parallel()\n\n           cases := []struct {\n               a, b Point\n               want float64\n           }{\n               {Point{0, 0}, Point{0, 0}, 0},\n               {Point{0, 0}, Point{3, 4}, 5},\n               {Point{1, 1}, Point{1, 1}, 0},\n               {Point{-1, -1}, Point{2, 3}, 5},\n           }\n\n           for _, c := range cases {\n               if got := Dist(c.a, c.b); got != c.want {\n                   t.Errorf(\"Dist(%v, %v) = %v, want %v\", c.a, c.b, got, c.want)\n               }\n           }\n       }\n       ```\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors were encountered. Both `Write` tool calls succeeded on the first attempt, and `go test ./...` passed immediately with no compilation or test failures. No user corrections or feedback were given on this task.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Located the existing `Point` type via Glob + Read before writing `Dist`, to ensure correct field names/types were used.\n   - Implemented `Dist` using standard Euclidean distance via `math.Sqrt`.\n   - Wrote a table-driven test covering: identical points (distance 0, two cases) and two distinct 3-4-5 right-triangle cases (distance 5), ensuring compliance with the house rule (`TestSpec_` prefix, `t.Parallel()` first).\n   - Ran `go test ./...` from the project root via Bash; output: `ok  \texample.com/geo/geo\t0.795s`, confirming the implementation and test pass with no errors.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - \"House rule for this session: every test function